{"caseId":"OD2-HO-KNOWN-2","methodChoice":"Collected two items. X8 splits the FCR fall by contact reason, referral status and tenure. X1 is the Finance change record, which gives the mechanism. I also compared the date of each April change with the weekly FCR series and checked that X8's figures reconcile to the site averages.","answers":[{"itemId":"S01","answer":"contradicted","confidence":90,"evidenceIds":["X8","E6","E2"]},{"itemId":"S02","answer":"supported","confidence":93,"evidenceIds":["X1","X8","E3"]},{"itemId":"S03","answer":"contradicted","confidence":88,"evidenceIds":["E2","E3","X8"]},{"itemId":"S04","answer":"contradicted","confidence":80,"evidenceIds":["X8","E2"]},{"itemId":"S05","answer":"contradicted","confidence":92,"evidenceIds":["X8","E2","E3"]},{"itemId":"S06","answer":"causal","confidence":90,"evidenceIds":["X1","X8","E3"]},{"itemId":"S07","answer":"causal","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["X8","E4"]},{"itemId":"S08","answer":"contradicted","confidence":87,"evidenceIds":["X8","E6","E2"]},{"itemId":"S09","answer":"association-only","confidence":62,"evidenceIds":["E5","E2"]},{"itemId":"S10","answer":"preferred","confidence":88,"evidenceIds":["X1","X8"]},{"itemId":"S11","answer":"harmful","confidence":92,"evidenceIds":["X8","E6","E1"]},{"itemId":"S12","answer":"premature","confidence":60,"evidenceIds":["X1"]},{"itemId":"S13","answer":"acceptable","confidence":55,"evidenceIds":["X8"]},{"itemId":"S14","answer":"sufficient","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["X1","X8"]}],"brief":"The fall is not mainly about the April starters, the tariff rise, the IVR or workload. On 14 April Finance cut the amount an agent can credit during a call from £100 to £25, after an audit finding. Anything bigger is now automatically referred to Billing Resolution. The share of billing calls referred jumped from 7% to 54% that week. Referred calls are resolved first time only about a third of the time (82% otherwise), largely because customers ring back to chase. That alone reproduces the whole drop. Tenured agents fell as far as the new starters, who are under a point lower; tariff calls resolve at 85%; the drop was complete before the IVR changed. Customer Operations wasn't consulted.

I'm about 90% sure of the cause; the link to complaints is only a coincidence in timing.

Next: drop the performance-plan proposal, which would penalise people for a rule change. Agree a revised in-call limit with Finance, backed by post-call sampling, and trial it on two teams for six weeks, tracking FCR and unsupported credits. Finance has said it would consider this. Use MI's one-day reruns for tracking rather than a three-month dashboard rebuild."}
